    "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::turso-result-error-never-checked": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::turso-result-error-never-checked",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "TursoResult.error is set on every DB failure but never checked by CRUD callers \u2014 outages surface as empty results/404s",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "error_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "legacy/cowabunga_api/data/database/turso_client.py",
          "legacy/cowabunga_api/data/crud_base.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "turso_client.py:169-172 \u2014 execute() catches httpx.HTTPError and broad Exception and returns TursoResult(data=[], error=str(e)) instead of raising",
          "Grep shows result.error is consumed only by TursoQueryBuilder.single() (turso_client.py:235); CRUDBase.get/update/list/create/delete read only result.data (crud_base.py:154,181,209,236), and TursoClient._execute_raw_sql callers (table_columns, health_check) likewise ignore it",
          "Downstream, routers translate the empty result into not-found, e.g. routers/openai/vector_stores.py:91-99 returns VectorStore | None and messages/threads raise 404 \u2014 a dead sqld is indistinguishable from empty tables"
        ],
        "suggestion": "Make the failure channel real: raise a DatabaseError from TursoQueryBuilder.execute() (and _execute_raw_sql) on HTTP/parse failure, or have CRUDBase check result.error and raise before interpreting empty data as not-found. Either way, finish the Result-type design or drop the unused error field.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "d1d57890"
      },
      "status": "open",
