        ],
        "evidence": [
          "turso_auth.py:91,123,129,141,162,172,186,188,203,208,220,348,352 \u2014 every auth failure path is `raise Exception('<message>')`, no shared error type",
          "crud_base.py:276 \u2014 get_current_user raises bare Exception('No authenticated user'); crud_base.py:261-265 converts ANY exception from db.auth.get_user() into user_id='anonymous', silently degrading auth-layer bugs",
          "routers/database_session.py:40-43,56-67 maps token/key problems to HTTP 401/403 \u2014 the same failure class gets a 500 or silent anonymous at the CRUD layer and a proper 401 only at the session layer"
        ],
        "suggestion": "Introduce one AuthError (or reuse Unauthorized) in the data layer, raise it from turso_auth/turso_client/crud_base auth paths, and map it to 401 in init_database_client; remove the except-Exception-to-anonymous fallback so unexpected auth failures propagate loudly.",
