      "id": "review::.::holistic::abstraction_fitness::turso-rpc-shim-single-impl-abcs",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "Post-Supabase, the DatabaseClient ABC layer, unused DatabaseConfig, and rpc() string-dispatch with ~130 lines of RPC wrapper classes serve exactly two internal call sites",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "abstraction_fitness",
        "related_files": [
          "legacy/cowabunga_api/data/database/base.py",
          "legacy/cowabunga_api/data/database/turso_client.py",
          "legacy/cowabunga_api/data/crud_vector_content.py",
          "legacy/cowabunga_api/data/crud_api_key.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "base.py:10-108 defines QueryBuilder, AuthClient, and DatabaseClient ABCs whose only remaining implementation is the Turso client (the Supabase client was deleted; zero supabase references remain in legacy/cowabunga_api/data/) - a one-implementation interface with no extension pressure.",
          "base.py:111-114 DatabaseConfig is referenced nowhere in the codebase, and its field comment '# or \"turso\"' duplicates the default value - a leftover of the two-backend design.",
          "turso_client.py:375-387 TursoClient.rpc() dispatches on a function-name string to _MatchVectorsRPC (lines 457-567) and _InsertAPIKeyRPC (lines 570-591), which exist solely for crud_vector_content.py:125 db.rpc('match_vectors', params).execute() and crud_api_key.py:77 db.rpc('insert_api_key', ...).execute(); params travel as dicts keyed by magic strings ('vs_id', 'p_user_id', ...).",
          "The rpc(...).execute() chain emulates a PostgREST RPC surface that no longer exists anywhere in the repo; callers hop through a generic string-dispatch facade plus a wrapper object before reaching the two SQL statements that are the real logic."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Replace the two rpc() call sites with direct typed async methods on TursoClient (e.g. match_vectors(query_embedding, vector_store_id, k, user_id) and insert_api_key(...named fields...)), delete _MatchVectorsRPC/_InsertAPIKeyRPC and the rpc() dispatcher, drop unused DatabaseConfig, and either delete the now-single-implementation ABCs in base.py or reduce them to the small surface CRUD actually calls (table/select/eq/execute, auth, options). If legacy Python is treated as frozen pending the Rust migration, record this as tracked debt there rather than refactoring.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "7c2960ee"
      },
