    "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::turso-execute-errors-degrade-to-empty-results": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::turso-execute-errors-degrade-to-empty-results",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "DB errors cross the seam as empty data: execute() swallows exceptions into TursoResult.error that no CRUD caller checks",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "mid_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "legacy/cowabunga_api/data/database/turso_client.py",
          "legacy/cowabunga_api/data/crud_base.py",
          "legacy/cowabunga_api/data/crud_vector_content.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "data/database/turso_client.py:169-172 - execute() catches httpx.HTTPError and bare Exception, returning TursoResult(data=[], error=str(e)) instead of raising.",
          "data/crud_base.py:142-238 - get/list/update/delete all read only result.data; none inspect result.error, so 'DB down' and 'no rows' produce identical None/[]/False outcomes (routers then emit 404).",
          "data/crud_vector_content.py:125-128 - similarity_search also ignores result.error; combined with _MatchVectorsRPC's silent brute-force fallback, vector search failure is indistinguishable from an empty store.",
          "The only .error consumer in the codebase is TursoQueryBuilder.single() at turso_client.py:235, so the error field is a dead contract for every other caller."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Make the failure contract explicit at one point: raise a DatabaseError from TursoQueryBuilder.execute() (and the rpc wrappers) when the transport fails or first['error'] is present, and delete the now-unreachable error-swallowing branches. Callers keep working unchanged because their code paths already assume data-or-nothing; where 'not found' must stay distinguishable, catch the new error in CRUDBase and return None deliberately. Do not add a second error convention.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "689b2c59"
      },
      "status": "open",
      "note": null,
