    "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::grpc-client-count-tokens-dead-sync-wrapper": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::grpc-client-count-tokens-dead-sync-wrapper",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "grpc_client.count_tokens is an uncalled sync-over-async wrapper whose except-Exception fallback silently returns a heuristic token count",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "mid_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "legacy/cowabunga_api/backend/grpc_client.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "backend/grpc_client.py:194-203 - count_tokens(model, text) imports asyncio inside the body, calls asyncio.get_event_loop().run_until_complete(create_token_count(...)), and on ANY exception returns max(1, len(text.split()) + 10) with no logging.",
          "Zero callers: the only imports of this module reference create_token_count (routers/cowabunga/tokens.py:3, routers/cowabunga/count.py:10); the SDK-side count_tokens in legacy/cowabunga_sdk/llm.py:54-55 is a different, legitimate contract.",
          "As written it is a trap for the next developer: the silent heuristic fallback means a future caller gets plausible-but-wrong token counts with no signal when the backend is down."
        ],
