        "evidence": [
          "base.py DatabaseClient declares only table/auth/options/create; rpc exists solely on TursoClient (turso_client.py:375).",
          "crud_api_key.py:77 and crud_vector_content.py:125 call `self.db.rpc(...)` unconditionally, so any non-Turso DatabaseClient implementation fails with AttributeError at runtime.",
          "crud_base.py:95 shows the inconsistency: it defensively checks `hasattr(self.db, \"table_columns\")` for another concrete-only method - two different strategies for the same ABC gap in the same layer.",
          "Related wontfix debt (unequal query-builder surfaces) shares this root cause but the ABC-vs-caller contract gap is a distinct, sharper defect."
        ],
