        ],
        "evidence": [
          "CRUDBase.update scopes every update with `query.eq('user_id', current_user['user_id'])` unless admin (crud_base.py:204-207).",
          "CRUDRun.update (crud_run.py:14-27) and CRUDVectorStore.update (crud_vector_store.py:62-76) re-implement update as `table.update(dict_).eq('id', id_)` with no user scoping; CRUDVectorStore.update additionally strips usage_bytes. Today's callers (runs.py modify_run, runs_steps cancel/submit, index.py modify_existing_vector_store) pre-check ownership via scoped gets, so the hole is latent - any future caller that updates by id directly performs a cross-tenant write."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Restore the base-class contract in both overrides: fetch current_user via self.get_current_user() and append `.eq('user_id', ...)` when not admin (or delegate to super().update after shaping the dict), so all tables in the domain inherit the same row-level authorization.",
