          "legacy/cowabunga_api/data/crud_vector_store.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "TursoQueryBuilder.execute (turso_client.py:150-172) catches all exceptions and returns TursoResult(data=[], error=...); _execute_sql/_execute_insert do the same for SQL-level errors (lines 139-140, 197-198)",
          "Grep confirms .error is read in exactly one place: TursoQueryBuilder.single() (turso_client.py:235); every CRUD callsite (e.g. crud_base.py:154, 181, 209, 236; crud_vector_store.py:68) only reads result.data",
          "Consequence: a failed INSERT/UPDATE (constraint violation, missing table) returns data=[] and CRUDBase.create/update return None - indistinguishable from 'row not found', so routers report 404/500-with-wrong-cause"
        ],
        "suggestion": "In CRUDBase (create/get/list/update/delete), check result.error after each execute() and raise a DataLayerError carrying the message instead of returning None on failure; alternatively make TursoQueryBuilder.execute raise on error and drop the error field, matching the raising contract the CRUD layer was written against.",
